"""Rorke's Drift: Natal, 22-23 January 1879.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

The afternoon of Isandlwana.  At the mission station by the drift over
the Buffalo River, a company of the 24th Foot, a few commissariat men
and the sick in the hospital have an hour's warning that the Zulu
reserve is coming: three or four thousand men under Prince
Dabulamanzi.  Lieutenants Chard and Bromhead build a wall of mealie bags
and biscuit boxes between the hospital and the storehouse, and wait.
Play either side against the computer, or against a friend at the same
screen.

Run it with ./rorkes (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.rorkes.json.  ./rorkes --selftest checks the map and plays
a game between two computer players.
"""

